.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-DOMAIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-domain - Serve a tunnel at hostnames under your workspace's domains


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel domain [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve a tunnel at hostnames under your workspace's domains

.PP
Serve a durable tunnel at your own hostnames. A hostname must be one level under a verified workspace domain (pb domain add); it needs no DNS step of its own.

.PP
Durable tunnels retain identity, routes, and domains across client sessions. Ephemeral tunnels have a separate lifecycle. Route publication and browser HTTP access require exact authorization; TLS for browser HTTP terminates at the edge.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for domain


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP, \fBpb-tunnel-domain-add(1)\fP, \fBpb-tunnel-domain-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-tunnel-domain-remove(1)\fP
